0 NOTE Pedigree-collapse fixture (TRD 12.1 — the centerpiece acceptance gate).
1 CONT An asymmetric cousin marriage: focal person Paul (@I11@) descends from the
1 CONT root couple Alfred (@I1@) and Bertha (@I2@) by TWO distinct lineages of
1 CONT DIFFERENT length, so each root ancestor is a pedigree-collapse point that
1 CONT implies two relationships at two different generations.
1 CONT
1 CONT Paternal line (3 generations up to a root):  Paul -> George -> Charles -> Alfred/Bertha
1 CONT Maternal line (4 generations up to a root):  Paul -> Helen  -> Xavier  -> Diana -> Alfred/Bertha
1 CONT
1 CONT EXPECTED (documented acceptance values, asserted in the tests):
1 CONT   detectPedigreeCollapse(@I11@) -> exactly 2 collapse points: @I1@ and @I2@.
1 CONT   enumeratePaths(@I11@, @I1@) -> exactly 2 paths:
1 CONT       [I11,I7,I3,I1] (len 3)   and   [I11,I10,I8,I4,I1] (len 4)
1 CONT   enumeratePaths(@I11@, @I2@) -> exactly 2 paths:
1 CONT       [I11,I7,I3,I2] (len 3)   and   [I11,I10,I8,I4,I2] (len 4)
1 CONT   Alfred (@I1@) is Paul's great-grandfather via the paternal line (gen 3)
1 CONT   and his 2nd great-grandfather via the maternal line (gen 4).
1 CONT   minimal.ged-style sanity: no OTHER individual is reached more than once.
